Sval: offer an agent tab's featureless new window to the chrome as a tab

A page in an agent's tab that opens a link under browser.link.open_newwindow
2, or with Shift held, gets a new window that Firefox opens in native code
with no chrome JS on the way (nsWindowWatcher::GetWindowOpenLocation, then
OpenWindowWithRemoteTab), so the window opens and takes focus before Sval can
put its content in the agent's own window. This offers such an open from a
tab Sval marks as an agent's (the SvalAgentTab field) to the chrome's
createContentWindowInFrame first, still as OPEN_NEWWINDOW. Sval's chrome opens
it as a background tab in the agent's window, or returns no element, and the
window opens as it would have. A window asked for with window features is a
popup and is left to Firefox. No chrome API is consulted for where a window
opens.

